<title>CANADA: Canada commission details extra strong wheat data.</title>
<headline>Canada commission details extra strong wheat data.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Thursday detailed preliminary milling and baking test results for No1 Canada Western Extra Strong Wheat.</p>
<p>PRELIMINARY DATA ON No1 Canada Western Extra Strong Wheat</p>
<p>Quality Parameters		 1996	     1995</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>  Test weight (kg/hl)	    80.2	     77.8</p>
<p>  Weight per 1,000 kernels, g  41.9	     38.6</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	  12.2	     12.4</p>
<p>  Dry Matter Protein (pct)     14.1	     14.3</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 1.51	     1.62</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g 6.5		8.0</p>
<p>  Falling Number		  360		350</p>
<p>  Flour Yield (pct)		76.1	     75.8</p>
<p>  PSI (pct)			  48		 48</p>
<p>FLOUR</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	  11.5	     11.9</p>
<p>  Wet Gluten Content (pct)     27.4	     32.5</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 0.57	     0.57</p>
<p>  Grade Colour, K-J units	-0.7	     -0.2</p>
<p>  AGTRON Colour (pct)	    61		 57</p>
<p>  Starch damage, Megazyme units 8.0	     n/a</p>
<p>  Starch damage, AACC units    12.2	     12.5</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g 2.5		3.5</p>
<p>  Amylograph Peak Viscosity, BU 560		405</p>
<p>  Maltose Value, g/100 g	  2.8		3.2</p>
<p>  Zeleny Sedimentation, mL     63		 64</p>
<p>FARINOGRAM</p>
<p>  Absorption (pct)		 63.2	     63.1</p>
<p>  Development Time, (90 rpms)   6.00 minutes   5.00</p>
<p>N.B.: unless otherwise noted, data based on 13.5 pct wheat moisture and 14.0 pct flour moisture.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
